cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "Please cite this research software release when using the accompanying implementations, predictions, analyses, or supplementary evidence."
type: software
title: "One-Sided Data Augmentation Pits Sensitivity against Invariance in Aspect-Based Sentiment Analysis: Research Software and Supplementary Evidence"
abstract: >-
  Research software and supporting experimental evidence accompanying the
  manuscript One-Sided Data Augmentation Pits Sensitivity against Invariance
  in Aspect-Based Sentiment Analysis. The archive covers four studies of
  robustness transfer: 174 controlled encoder runs, 122 augmentation-strategy
  runs, 64 in-context-learning inference jobs, and 24 LoRA fine-tuning runs
  plus two zero-shot evaluations. It includes study implementations,
  source-text-free frozen prediction records, numerical summaries,
  supplementary Tables S1–S16, and offline verification utilities.
